{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27282648","formula":"C₂₄H₁₆F₃NO₄","hill":"C24H16F3NO4","elements":["H","C","N","O","F"],"composition":{"C":24.0,"F":3.0,"H":16.0,"N":1.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Tiplasinin"},"descriptions":{"en":"Tiplasinin (INNTooltip International Nonproprietary Name, USANTooltip United States Adopted Name) or tiplaxtinin (PAI-039) is a drug which acts as an inhibitor of the serpin protein plasminogen activator inhibitor-1 (PAI-1), thereby increasing activity of the enzymes tissue plasminogen activator and urokinase, which are involved in the blood clotting cascade. Inhibition of PAI-1 can help to prevent damage to blood vessel walls that occurs as a consequence of chronic high blood pressure, as well as preventing the formation of blood clots that can lead to stroke and heart attack, and potentially also providing a novel treatment mechanism to slow the development of diabetes and obesity."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":6450819,"mass":439.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C(C=C1)CN2C=C(C3=C2C=CC(=C3)C4=CC=C(C=C4)OC(F)(F)F)C(=O)C(=O)O","inchikey":"ODXQFEWQSHNQNI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-[1-benzyl-5-[4-(trifluoromethoxy)phenyl]indol-3-yl]-2-oxoacetic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6450819","atoms":48,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":6.322,"y":0.156,"z":-1.864,"el":"F"},{"x":8.23,"y":-0.766,"z":-1.331,"el":"F"},{"x":7.574,"y":1.026,"z":-0.265,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.732,"y":3.775,"z":0.296,"el":"O"},{"x":6.513,"y":-0.963,"z":0.121,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.297,"y":5.187,"z":-0.914,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.892,"y":3.532,"z":-0.984,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.109,"y":-0.044,"z":1.091,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.781,"y":-0.399,"z":1.017,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.072,"y":0.739,"z":0.626,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.021,"y":1.788,"z":0.469,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.195,"y":-0.926,"z":1.461,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.264,"y